.TH UNSETENV 1 "OShell Built-in Commands"
.SH NAME
unsetenv \- delete an environment variable
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unsetenv
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B unsetenv
command removes an environment variable from the shell's environment.
.PP
If the variable does not exist, the command does nothing (no error).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B NAME
The name of the environment variable to remove.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B unsetenv EDITOR
Remove the EDITOR variable.
.TP
.B unsetenv MYVAR
Remove the MYVAR variable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on error.
.SH ERRORS
Prints "An error has occurred" if incorrect number of arguments (must be exactly 1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setenv (1),
.BR env (1),
.BR bash (1)